    "display_title": "docs(decisions): Decisions 159 and 160, spec 39 step 10: a 25k-a-side target, work that follows change, then threads, off the main thread",
    "event": "pull_request",
    "head_branch": "chore/spec-39-step-10-design",
    "head_commit_message": "perf(native): parting's sums measured, not kept; step 10 closed (spec 39 step 10f) (#742)\n\n* perf(native): sum parting's pushes per body on the pool, in pair order\n\nEach pass's pushes become keys (body, pair, side), sorted on the pool, so\neach body's pushes run together in pair order. Each body's run is summed\nfrom zero on the pool and the bodies are moved in the order the serial\npass first meets them, so outcomes are bit for bit the same. Coincident\npairs still ask the seeded way on this thread, in pair order. The\none-thread path keeps the serial sums.\n\nRefs #557\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi4zcfHZcGHMi4aC5yB\n\n* docs(spec): record step 10f and close step 10 (spec 39)\n\nParting's sums on the pool, and what 10f's options came to (#738):\nthe cadence not built, f32 columns parked, a different reduction order\nnot needed, positions in f64 as debt (#740). Names the next design\nsession. Bench numbers to follow.\n\nRefs #557\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi4zcfHZcGHMi4aC5yB\n\n* perf(native): keep parting's sums serial, the pooled ones benched slower\n\nBench runs #81 and #82 against 10e's branch, 5 rounds: parting went\n51.49 -> 62.35 ms at 25k (+21%) and 8.44 -> 10.89 ms at 4096 (+29%),\nranges apart. The serial adds are about 2 ms a pass; the pair search,\nalready threaded, is the cost. The identity guard stays. The spec\nrecords the measurement and closes step 10.\n\nRefs #557\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi4zcfHZcGHMi4aC5yB\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
